AltoBorrowMarket::AddSupply()
├── when market is paused
│   └── it should revert
├── when market is frozen
│   └── it should revert
├── given invalid inputs
│   ├── when both assets and shares are zero
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when both assets and shares are non-zero
│   │   └── it should revert
│   └── when onBehalf is zero address
│       └── it should revert
├
└── given valid inputs
    ├── when user has insufficient balance
    │   └── it should revert
    └── when user has sufficient balance
        ├── when assets is zero
        │   ├── it should calculate assets from shares
        │   └── it should add supply shares to position
        ├── when shares is zero
        │   ├── it should calculate shares from assets
        │   └── it should add supply shares to position
        ├── when supply cap is exceeded
        │   └── it should revert
        ├── it should emit AccrueInterest
        ├── it should update totalSupply
        ├── it should not update totalBorrowed
        ├── it should transfer borrow tokens from sender
        ├── it should emit AddSupply event
        ├── it should add supply shares to position
        └── it should return the amount of assets and shares added